    {
      "id": "s28",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "We realized that they must have become unduly frightened by the rising flood, for their house, which had sound foundations, would have stood stoutly even if it had been almost submerged.",
      "translation": "我们意识到，他们一定是被不断上涨的洪水吓得不轻。因为他们的房子地基稳固，即便几乎被淹没，也能屹立不倒。",
      "startTime": 185.9,
      "endTime": 200.41,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "unduly",
            "pos": "adv.",
